WEBVTT

00:16.990 --> 00:18.030
Yorito!

00:18.620 --> 00:19.290
I'm all right.

00:19.540 --> 00:20.750
More importantly, how is Matsuri?

00:21.000 --> 00:21.790
Yorito?

00:22.870 --> 00:24.580
I've found a way.

00:25.210 --> 00:28.920
Maybe now we can bring you under the sky!

00:41.810 --> 00:44.350
...this is bad no matter how you look at it...

00:52.320 --> 00:53.440
You're so warm...

01:09.290 --> 01:15.710
hane ga shiroku hikari mabushiku tondeyuku

01:09.290 --> 01:15.710
White feathers gleam and fly away brightly

01:16.130 --> 01:22.760
kokoro dake nosete hoshii no ni

01:16.130 --> 01:22.760
Though I only want to set my heart on them

01:23.760 --> 01:30.020
tsumetai te wo nobasu todokanai... shitteru

01:23.760 --> 01:30.020
I extend my cold hands - They won't reach... I know

01:30.650 --> 01:37.740
dakedo ima furetai kimi ni

01:30.650 --> 01:37.740
But I want to touch you now

01:37.950 --> 01:43.870
natsukashii kaze ni ha ano koro no fune

01:37.950 --> 01:43.870
On that nostalgic wind - A ship from the past

01:44.280 --> 01:52.290
maboroshi ga omoide wo miseta

01:44.280 --> 01:52.290
An illusion showed me memories

01:53.360 --> 02:02.300
"wasurenai" dareka no koe ga setsunaku hibiku

01:53.360 --> 02:02.300
"I won't forget" Someone's voice echoes painfully

02:02.470 --> 02:07.390
hajimaru yokan ni furuete

02:02.470 --> 02:07.390
Trembling with a foreboding

02:07.680 --> 02:15.730
"wasuretai" negau jibun ga wakaranai

02:07.680 --> 02:15.730
"I want to forget" I cannot understand myself for hoping so

02:16.110 --> 02:25.450
matteiru yurarenagara yume hitotsu wo

02:16.110 --> 02:25.450
I shall wait while swaying, for that one dream

02:32.040 --> 02:37.000
Blood of a Sacrifice

02:33.040 --> 02:37.300
Then that man might come and attack you again!

02:37.970 --> 02:41.680
I managed to injure him a bit, so I think I should be safe for now.

02:42.220 --> 02:44.760
He probably won't be able to move his arm any time soon.

02:45.100 --> 02:46.430
I see...

02:48.180 --> 02:49.060
What's wrong?

02:49.390 --> 02:52.770
You know that I'm not human, right?

02:52.770 --> 02:55.400
Yeah, you're called a Yaka, correct?

02:55.400 --> 02:56.780
I've heard all about it.

02:57.440 --> 02:58.900
Everything's okay then.

02:59.280 --> 03:02.160
I was somehow prepared for this.

03:02.160 --> 03:03.280
Prepared?

03:04.120 --> 03:07.750
Yorito wouldn't let just any girl stay at his place.

03:08.120 --> 03:11.080
So I knew that there was some kind of reason behind it.

03:11.330 --> 03:12.290
Besides...

03:13.420 --> 03:15.800
It's not like I hate you.

03:19.470 --> 03:20.380
I see.

03:22.220 --> 03:23.300
Wait... where's Yorito?

03:23.300 --> 03:24.220
Wait... where's Yorito?

03:25.180 --> 03:26.310
Oh no!

03:26.970 --> 03:28.270
Yorito!

03:28.270 --> 03:30.940
Yorito, it's time to go to school.

03:30.140 --> 03:32.020
I'll go in the afternoon.

03:30.940 --> 03:32.020
Yorito!

03:32.770 --> 03:36.320
I woke up early today to take a photo of the morning glow.

03:37.480 --> 03:39.110
Iron claw...

03:41.150 --> 03:42.200
Knock it off!

03:42.200 --> 03:44.450
They sure do get along well.

03:46.490 --> 03:47.620
Even though it's just slightly,

03:47.870 --> 03:50.450
there are signs similar to necrosis on your arm.

03:50.620 --> 03:51.410
Necrosis?

03:51.750 --> 03:52.790
How did that happen?

03:53.290 --> 03:55.630
Probably because I slept on my arm.

03:55.630 --> 03:56.750
It's nothing really important.

03:56.750 --> 03:58.210
No, you can't get it from slee-

03:58.500 --> 04:00.300
My body's always been like that.

04:00.550 --> 04:02.420
Besides, something like this has happened to me before.

04:02.420 --> 04:03.800
But I left it alone and it healed over time.

04:04.140 --> 04:05.010
Regardless...

04:05.010 --> 04:06.720
She's such a big worrywart.

04:06.970 --> 04:08.350
Thank you for your time.

04:08.760 --> 04:09.270
Excuse me.

04:09.470 --> 04:10.600
Takeshi, wait...

04:11.100 --> 04:12.600
Takeshi, I said wait!

04:13.730 --> 04:16.190
I went to see the doctor, just like I said.

04:16.440 --> 04:17.900
You call that seeing a doctor?

04:17.900 --> 04:19.530
It's really nothing.

04:20.150 --> 04:22.110
Then tell me what happened.

04:23.200 --> 04:25.110
Something happened between you and the Yaka, didn't it?

04:25.570 --> 04:26.780
You're worrying too much.

04:27.160 --> 04:27.950
Hey! Wait, Takeshi!

04:27.950 --> 04:29.790
Hey! Wait, Takeshi!

04:34.000 --> 04:36.130
I'm truly sorry about that.

04:36.130 --> 04:37.670
Watch where you're going! Geez!

04:38.130 --> 04:38.920
Takeshi!

04:45.930 --> 04:49.140
I'm very sorry for being late.

04:49.310 --> 04:50.100
Um... I called Mana-san and-

04:50.100 --> 04:52.390
Um... I called Mana-san and-

04:53.350 --> 04:54.350
It's Onee-chan.

04:54.560 --> 04:55.020
R-Right... sorry.

04:55.020 --> 04:55.560
R-Right... sorry.

04:55.560 --> 04:56.980
R-Right... sorry.

04:57.190 --> 04:58.770
Anyway, as I was saying,

04:58.770 --> 05:01.530
they said they had something to discuss with you,

05:01.530 --> 05:04.700
and that they're coming over to visit tomorrow if it rains.

05:05.610 --> 05:06.450
If it rains?

05:06.450 --> 05:07.200
That's right.

05:07.200 --> 05:10.490
They said they'd explain the details when they come over.

05:16.330 --> 05:19.790
If you're just like this when you come to school, then it's no different from staying at home!

05:20.130 --> 05:20.920
Sorry. Just give me a minute.

05:20.920 --> 05:21.920
Sorry. Just give me a minute.

05:22.210 --> 05:23.590
I have a good shot.

05:23.960 --> 05:24.990
A good shot?

05:25.630 --> 05:28.590
The sun was peeking out from behind the clouds.

05:29.890 --> 05:31.310
Is this for Matsuri-san?

05:31.310 --> 05:31.970
Yeah.

05:32.350 --> 05:35.730
I thought I'd show her what the sun looks like.

05:36.020 --> 05:37.230
I even dried the futon.

05:37.480 --> 05:38.190
The futon?

05:39.520 --> 05:40.900
I see.

05:42.690 --> 05:44.240
...I promise you.

05:44.570 --> 05:45.490
Got it.

05:45.740 --> 05:47.610
I won't go outside anymore...

05:48.030 --> 05:50.780
...until you show me the sky.

05:57.620 --> 05:58.960
Say, Yorito.

05:59.540 --> 06:03.250
Are you really going to introduce her to Aono-san tomorrow?

06:03.880 --> 06:04.460
Yeah.

06:05.130 --> 06:07.720
I can't hide it any longer.

06:08.590 --> 06:10.340
Who will you introduce her as?

06:13.180 --> 06:14.600
Well... as a friend, I guess.

06:14.600 --> 06:16.480
Well... as a friend, I guess.

06:16.850 --> 06:19.900
Do you think Aono-san will be satisfied with that?

06:20.350 --> 06:22.730
She's not like me, you know.

06:23.230 --> 06:24.070
Is that so?

06:24.070 --> 06:26.780
Try looking at things from her perspective.

06:26.780 --> 06:30.070
If Aono-san brought a guy
home that you've never met,

06:30.070 --> 06:33.910
and said, "This is my friend. From now on he'll be living with us,"

06:33.910 --> 06:35.120
would you accept that?

06:37.000 --> 06:37.790
Really... You don't think about anything.

06:37.790 --> 06:39.790
Really... You don't think about anything.

06:40.120 --> 06:42.500
Then what should I tell her?

06:42.790 --> 06:46.340
This might be a little straightforward, but it's the only way possible.

06:46.840 --> 06:47.630
The only way?

06:49.510 --> 06:50.590
Yup!

06:52.550 --> 06:53.510
As lovers?

06:53.800 --> 06:54.680
No. I actually said as friends.

06:54.680 --> 06:57.430
No. I actually said as friends.

06:57.640 --> 07:01.690
But then Mana said we'll be able to persuade her better this way.

07:01.900 --> 07:02.650
All right.

07:02.980 --> 07:04.320
I'm fine with that.

07:05.360 --> 07:06.440
Really?

07:06.730 --> 07:07.320
Yeah.

07:10.990 --> 07:11.990
What's that?

07:13.450 --> 07:16.040
The sun somehow looks like an eye.

07:17.290 --> 07:19.710
People say it's the sky holding an umbrella.

07:19.710 --> 07:21.670
If you see this, it means it's going to rain tomorrow.

07:22.250 --> 07:23.250
I see.

07:23.250 --> 07:25.590
The weather forecast said it would rain too.

07:25.590 --> 07:26.210
Yeah.

07:26.800 --> 07:28.550
Well, let's practice.

07:28.840 --> 07:29.670
Practice?

07:29.920 --> 07:30.800
Yup.

07:31.220 --> 07:34.390
I'm going to be your girlfriend, remember?

07:43.690 --> 07:44.980
I'll go prepare your futon.

08:06.170 --> 08:08.130
The smell of the sun?

08:09.130 --> 08:09.800
Yeah.

08:10.170 --> 08:13.130
A sun-dried futon smells just like the sun.

08:13.550 --> 08:15.390
The smell of the sun...

08:15.390 --> 08:15.970
Yup.

08:15.970 --> 08:17.220
You do it like this.

08:19.930 --> 08:21.770
Like this...

08:24.060 --> 08:25.350
It's kind of warm.

08:25.350 --> 08:26.060
Isn't it?

08:26.440 --> 08:28.360
This is the warmth of the sun.

08:28.650 --> 08:30.280
The warmth of daylight.

08:30.730 --> 08:31.900
So this is it...

08:33.950 --> 08:34.700
That was fast!

08:42.910 --> 08:46.290
I'm going to be your girlfriend, remember?

08:47.500 --> 08:48.540
No way...

08:49.130 --> 08:49.920
What?

08:50.210 --> 08:51.300
Don't let go.

08:54.880 --> 08:57.180
It feels nice and warm.

08:58.640 --> 08:59.890
Hey, Yorito.

09:01.180 --> 09:03.230
Is there someone you like?

09:04.690 --> 09:05.600
So there is someone.

09:05.600 --> 09:07.310
N-Not really.

09:07.900 --> 09:08.730
Oh?

09:09.020 --> 09:10.860
Then... let's kiss.

09:10.860 --> 09:12.190
Then... let's kiss.

09:16.110 --> 09:17.490
Don't tease me.

09:17.780 --> 09:19.530
Does it look like I'm teasing you?

09:40.760 --> 09:41.850
Why you...

09:43.140 --> 09:45.230
You were serious!

09:45.230 --> 09:46.390
Why you...!

09:47.560 --> 09:49.350
Of course I was kidding!

09:49.810 --> 09:50.400
Hold it!

09:50.520 --> 09:52.230
I'm looking forward to tomorrow.

09:52.480 --> 09:55.150
There's a lot I want to tell your sister.

09:55.150 --> 09:56.570
You don't have to tell her anything!

09:56.570 --> 10:01.240
You'll just say, "Pleased to meet you, Aono-neesan. I'm Shihou Matsuri."

10:01.740 --> 10:02.660
Aono?

10:02.660 --> 10:03.740
Got it?

10:04.620 --> 10:07.410
Your sister's name is Aono?

10:08.750 --> 10:10.830
Oh, didn't I mention it?

10:13.550 --> 10:15.210
Morimiya... Aono...

10:15.210 --> 10:16.630
Morimiya... Aono...

10:25.640 --> 10:30.150
She usually wakes up at the slightest sound.

10:30.150 --> 10:33.110
Well, we shouldn't wake her when she's sleeping.

10:33.110 --> 10:34.480
We should wait a little longer.

10:34.780 --> 10:36.650
Sorry about this, Matsuri.

10:39.400 --> 10:41.780
Then I'll go get some juice.

10:42.200 --> 10:43.120
Yeah.

10:47.160 --> 10:48.620
Matsuri, let's go.

10:49.330 --> 10:50.290
Yeah.

11:04.970 --> 11:05.970
Sorry.

11:05.970 --> 11:09.230
I didn't expect her to be asleep during visiting hours.

11:09.640 --> 11:10.690
It's okay.

11:10.690 --> 11:11.900
It couldn't be helped.

11:12.400 --> 11:14.650
Maybe she just pretended to be asleep.

11:15.020 --> 11:19.110
But she seemed to be sleeping so soundly...

11:19.110 --> 11:20.030
Say... is Aono-san...

11:20.030 --> 11:21.360
Say... is Aono-san...

11:21.910 --> 11:22.740
What is it?

11:23.030 --> 11:24.830
How long has she been hospitalized?

11:25.240 --> 11:26.200
Let's see...

11:26.580 --> 11:29.580
She collapsed when we moved here.

11:30.000 --> 11:31.620
So about three months.

11:31.620 --> 11:32.420
Yeah.

11:32.670 --> 11:35.670
I met Yorito at the hospital around that time.

11:35.670 --> 11:36.880
And before?

11:37.710 --> 11:38.960
She used to be fine.

11:39.340 --> 11:42.840
We don't know the reason why she's sick.

11:42.840 --> 11:46.760
The doctor said she just overworked herself.

11:46.760 --> 11:47.640
I see...

12:00.150 --> 12:00.990
Matsuri?

12:02.740 --> 12:04.240
I'll... walk home.

12:04.240 --> 12:05.410
I'll... walk home.

12:06.370 --> 12:09.490
It's been a while since I felt like walking through the town.

12:09.490 --> 12:10.500
I see.

12:10.660 --> 12:12.080
Don't be late.

12:12.370 --> 12:12.960
Okay.

12:43.240 --> 12:44.360
Geez...

12:45.240 --> 12:47.320
It gets worse every time...

12:51.370 --> 12:52.450
Geez!

12:55.830 --> 12:57.710
I guess I can't use it yet.

13:04.630 --> 13:06.930
So it was you after all.

13:18.520 --> 13:20.190
You knew?

13:21.110 --> 13:23.320
I heard about you from Koyori.

13:23.320 --> 13:24.700
She said your name was "Matsuri."

13:25.240 --> 13:26.280
I see...

13:27.110 --> 13:29.490
I've just recently regained my powers.

13:29.910 --> 13:32.200
The powers that I overused.

13:34.500 --> 13:36.620
So that's why you collapsed.

13:36.920 --> 13:41.090
There's no other reason why an eternal being, a Yaka, would be hospitalized.

13:41.550 --> 13:44.420
And during that time, you appeared.

13:47.050 --> 13:48.050
But it's fine.

13:48.720 --> 13:51.390
I knew one day this would happen.

13:52.720 --> 13:55.020
During this endless time we're living in...

14:02.860 --> 14:04.070
And Yorito?

14:04.530 --> 14:05.530
He's my brother.

14:05.530 --> 14:06.070
No way!

14:06.070 --> 14:07.200
That's impossible!

14:07.570 --> 14:08.530
But Yorito is...

14:08.530 --> 14:09.660
My brother.

14:11.030 --> 14:13.120
My one and only brother...

14:29.260 --> 14:30.010
W-Well... that's...

14:30.010 --> 14:30.840
W-Well... that's...

14:30.840 --> 14:32.050
W-Well... that's...

14:32.050 --> 14:33.600
Just give me a straight answer!

14:33.600 --> 14:35.310
Do you want to put it in or not?

14:35.310 --> 14:36.310
That's not fair!

14:36.310 --> 14:39.560
Since she's your sister, it's obvious she'll say the same thing as you.

14:39.560 --> 14:41.150
That's completely irrelevant!

14:41.310 --> 14:43.940
I've never heard of putting cabbage in sukiyaki.

14:43.940 --> 14:48.490
It's not sukiyaki if it doesn't have any cabbage in it!

14:48.780 --> 14:49.650
Um...

14:49.650 --> 14:53.030
Let's cook half and half.

14:53.030 --> 14:54.030
I'm back.

14:54.620 --> 14:55.580
Matsuri!

14:56.580 --> 14:57.750
Great timing!

14:58.080 --> 15:00.420
You put cabbage in sukiyaki, right?

15:00.420 --> 15:01.080
Right?

15:01.080 --> 15:02.790
You don't, right?

15:04.920 --> 15:05.920
I guess... you don't.

15:05.920 --> 15:06.670
I guess... you don't.

15:06.670 --> 15:07.760
See?

15:07.760 --> 15:08.920
That settles it!

15:08.970 --> 15:09.170
W-W-Wait, wait...

15:09.170 --> 15:09.470
W-W-Wait, wait...

15:09.470 --> 15:10.380
W-W-Wait, wait...

15:10.380 --> 15:10.970
You do.

15:14.470 --> 15:16.260
Sis?

15:19.310 --> 15:23.650
So, you came after us after hearing about us from the nurse?

15:24.440 --> 15:25.070
Yeah.

15:25.480 --> 15:28.820
She came out right after you guys got on the train.

15:29.280 --> 15:30.900
You don't need to push yourself.

15:31.200 --> 15:32.450
It's not good for your body.

15:32.950 --> 15:33.740
I'm fine.

15:34.070 --> 15:35.950
I wanted to eat meat, too.

15:36.410 --> 15:39.910
But is it okay for you not to return to the hospital?

15:39.910 --> 15:43.670
I got permission to stay here for a while.

15:43.670 --> 15:44.500
But-

15:44.500 --> 15:47.960
That's my condition for letting Matsuri-san stay here.

15:48.510 --> 15:50.090
Seems you lost, Yorito.

15:50.880 --> 15:52.340
Fine!

15:52.340 --> 15:54.550
I'll go talk to the teacher tomorrow.

15:54.850 --> 15:57.140
Now you can't do anything perverted.

15:57.140 --> 15:58.220
Of course not!

15:58.220 --> 16:00.230
I didn't do anything perverted to begin with!

16:00.230 --> 16:01.230
Really?

16:01.230 --> 16:03.480
There was that close call, though.

16:04.560 --> 16:04.980
D-Don't say nonsense like that!

16:04.980 --> 16:06.400
D-Don't say nonsense like that!

16:06.400 --> 16:07.770
When did I do such a thing?

16:08.110 --> 16:08.940
But you did.

16:08.940 --> 16:10.610
Yesterday, on the futon.

16:11.150 --> 16:13.610
You were the one inviting me to do so!

16:13.610 --> 16:14.570
Inviting?!

16:14.570 --> 16:15.870
So it's true after all!

16:15.870 --> 16:17.330
No, of course not!

16:17.490 --> 16:23.160
I'm deeply sorry, but I'm changing my impression of you, Yorito-san!

16:23.160 --> 16:24.420
But...

16:24.670 --> 16:26.000
By futon I meant...

16:26.000 --> 16:29.420
You know, when you dry it in the sun, it smells just like the sun, right?

16:29.420 --> 16:30.420
It was on that futon.

16:30.420 --> 16:32.260
What was going on in that futon?!

16:33.680 --> 16:35.180
Shall I walk you home?

16:35.180 --> 16:37.680
I respectfully reject that idea.

16:38.100 --> 16:39.140
Let's go, Koyori!

16:39.510 --> 16:40.930
Bye, perverted Yorito.

16:40.930 --> 16:41.980
As I said, I was-

16:47.860 --> 16:48.940
Hey...

16:52.610 --> 16:55.320
I have a single favor to ask of you.

17:10.250 --> 17:11.840
You poor thing.

17:12.170 --> 17:12.800
Here.

17:14.630 --> 17:15.720
I don't need it.

17:21.470 --> 17:23.930
It's kind of exciting.

17:24.350 --> 17:26.560
Does it really have to be tonight?

17:26.900 --> 17:29.440
If it's going inside, we can do it on any rainy Sund-

17:31.480 --> 17:33.110
But I want to go inside now.

17:33.320 --> 17:36.030
We'll run for it if someone sees us, okay?

17:36.450 --> 17:37.860
Yeah, okay.

17:48.170 --> 17:51.130
This window is a bit loose.

17:54.420 --> 17:56.510
It's more spacious than I thought.

17:56.510 --> 17:57.970
That's because no one else is here.

17:59.760 --> 18:03.060
It looks really small when it's filled with people.

18:06.600 --> 18:07.480
Is it here?

18:07.480 --> 18:08.140
Yeah.

18:12.270 --> 18:13.690
That's my seat.

18:14.030 --> 18:15.740
And this one's Mana's.

18:19.780 --> 18:21.490
So this is what it feels like.

18:22.780 --> 18:25.700
I've only seen this on TV.

18:26.000 --> 18:28.370
It really isn't that great.

18:28.370 --> 18:29.460
It's boring.

18:29.830 --> 18:33.670
The teacher is annoying, and the lessons make you sleepy.

18:34.750 --> 18:35.960
So you knew?

18:36.460 --> 18:38.130
The P.E. classes make me lazy.

18:38.380 --> 18:40.010
And I have to wake up early in the morning.

18:41.140 --> 18:42.350
But... at least you're not alone.

18:42.350 --> 18:43.390
But... at least you're not alone.

18:45.100 --> 18:46.600
That alone... is a blessing.

18:46.600 --> 18:48.140
That alone... is a blessing.

18:49.600 --> 18:50.560
So...

18:52.230 --> 18:54.070
Do you watch the sky from here?

18:55.110 --> 18:56.150
No.

18:56.530 --> 18:57.650
I watch it from...

19:02.370 --> 19:03.200
Here?

19:03.580 --> 19:04.240
Yeah.

19:04.910 --> 19:08.410
I lie down here and aim my camera at the sky.

19:12.210 --> 19:14.420
It's really beautiful.

19:14.420 --> 19:15.170
Don't you think so?

19:15.550 --> 19:18.260
It's the most peaceful place here.

19:18.630 --> 19:20.680
So when I'm asleep during the day,

19:20.680 --> 19:22.890
You lie down here as well?

19:23.140 --> 19:24.180
Well, yeah.

19:25.060 --> 19:26.890
While I'm sleeping...

19:27.720 --> 19:29.810
...you're living in a world unknown to me.

19:30.190 --> 19:32.020
It'll become a world you know.

19:34.190 --> 19:35.320
I'll... take you out.

19:35.320 --> 19:36.270
I'll... take you out.

19:54.460 --> 19:56.040
It's so peaceful.

19:57.130 --> 19:57.840
Yeah.

19:58.460 --> 19:59.800
It is late after all.

20:01.260 --> 20:02.010
Say...

20:03.300 --> 20:07.390
Do you know why people sleep?

20:09.640 --> 20:12.440
You know, when people sleep...

20:12.770 --> 20:17.110
...they throw away all their pain, anxieties and hatred.

20:19.280 --> 20:23.240
And they welcome the morning with a lightened heart.

20:23.700 --> 20:25.990
The pain fades into the darkness.

20:26.320 --> 20:31.250
The clear sky and the new day welcome people.

20:49.140 --> 20:55.230
Yakas are beings which were formed from the pain and anxiety that people threw into the night.

20:57.440 --> 21:01.690
They're their other selves they hated.

21:02.110 --> 21:04.650
Why did you bring me back to life?

21:05.360 --> 21:09.490
I don't want to live in a world without Yorito!

21:13.750 --> 21:14.870
That's why... Yakas are alone.

21:14.870 --> 21:16.290
That's why... Yakas are alone.

21:16.580 --> 21:17.630
Matsuri...

21:17.630 --> 21:19.920
They have to live alone.

21:19.920 --> 21:21.130
But that is...

21:21.130 --> 21:22.420
Yorito.

21:35.770 --> 21:36.640
I told you, didn't I?

21:37.060 --> 21:39.230
I wasn't teasing you.

21:47.740 --> 21:48.700
Matsuri...

22:14.310 --> 22:22.980
iro aseta page no kioku hitomi tojireba yomigaeru

22:14.310 --> 22:22.980
Memories on a faded page, they revive when I close my eyes

22:23.400 --> 22:32.160
adokenai shoujo no inori
habatakeyo kibou no sora he

22:23.400 --> 22:32.160
Prayers of an innocent girl
Fly away to the sky of hope

22:32.280 --> 22:36.580
nageku mamonaku  toki wa nagareru

22:32.280 --> 22:36.580
With no time to regret, time will flow

22:36.870 --> 22:41.670
hitori tachidomaru kedo

22:36.870 --> 22:41.670
Even though I stand alone

22:42.920 --> 22:48.430
yume mamoru shirabe  kuchizu samuno

22:42.920 --> 22:48.430
A tune to protect your dreams, I sing to myself

22:48.590 --> 22:52.930
hitobito ga nemuri ni tsukeba

22:48.590 --> 22:52.930
When people go into slumber

22:53.140 --> 23:00.850
mata au hi no negai tsumugeru deshou  ai no ito

22:53.140 --> 23:00.850
Their wish to unite can be woven. The thread of love

23:01.150 --> 23:11.280
yasashisa wo sasou  otogibanashi anata kara osowatta no yo

23:01.150 --> 23:11.280
Fairy tales that elicit kindness I learned that from you

23:11.450 --> 23:21.210
modorimashou  sotto ano koro no omoi ni

23:11.450 --> 23:21.210
